I("surgery","xsurg-compartment-tib","Surgery","Trauma","difficult","M",24,
 "the ward","tibial shaft fracture, casted, now severe pain, pain on passive stretch of the toes, paraesthesia",
 "pain not controlled with opioids",
 "Tense calf, pulses still present, pain on passive extension of toes.",
 "Compartment pressures not mandatory if the clinical picture is clear.",
 "What is the most appropriate action?",
 "Immediate fasciotomy (split/remove the cast on the way) — pulses can be present until late",
 ["Elevate and observe overnight because pulses are present","Increase the opioid PCA as the only action","Venous duplex as the first treatment","Ice and a tighter cast"],
 "Compartment syndrome is a clinical diagnosis: pain, stretch pain, paraesthesia. Pulses are a late sign. Fasciotomy saves the limb.",
 ["Pulses do not exclude it.","Pain is the disease, not the only treatment target.","Not a DVT primarily.","A tighter cast worsens it."],
 "If you think about fasciotomy, call the surgeon now.","Reassuring because the dorsalis pedis is present.","Fasciotomise clinical compartment syndrome.","BOAST / Australian orthopaedic trauma"),

